N2  - In order to achieve the interoperability among heterogeneous ontologies, ontology mapping is the most effective solution. Based on the investigation, comparison and analysis of current ontology mapping techniques, a view-based ontology mapping model on the basis of schema mapping theory is proposed. Firstly the local ontology views and cluster to the local information classes are constructed according to their semantic relations. Then, on the basis of analyzing the information semantic relations, the local information classes arc integrated into the global information classes to construct the global view and the mapping relationship between the global view and the local views. This model can make ontology mapping be comprehensible and clear, is suitable for dynamic information environment, and is helpful to establish a platform for sharing information of heterogeneous ontologies.
